Arrays of Objects
Deleting Arrays
    Always use delete on anything allocated with new, 
    and always use delete[] on anything allocated with new[].

    In modern C++ you should avoid using raw C-style pointers. 
    Instead of storing plain-old dumb pointers in C-style arrays, 
    you should store smart pointers in modern Standard Library containers. 
    Smart pointers automatically deallocate the memory associated with them at the right time.